<article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 text-apx-text sm:px-6 sm:py-14">
  <header class="mb-8">
    <p class="apx-mono-label">APX / Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-apx-muted">Last updated: 22 October 2026</p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-8 leading-7 text-apx-muted">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Information APX processes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Depending on the features you use, APX may process your email address, account and profile
        details, sign-in provider identifiers, optional phone-verification data, proposal and
        comment contributions, votes, delegation choices, newsletter preferences, and messages sent
        through the contact form. Public contributions may be shown on the service; account details
        and private settings are not all public.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The service also receives technical request data such as IP address, browser information,
        pages requested, timestamps, and security events. Operational logs are retained for a limited
        period for reliability, abuse prevention, and troubleshooting.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Votes, delegation, and Reconsider</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Direct votes and delegation settings are linked to an account so the platform can apply its
        voting rules. Reconsider may collect before-and-after responses and selected delegates;
        completed responses are linked to an account to prevent duplicate submissions and are
        presented as aggregate results. A participant's current response may also be recorded as an
        APX vote. Do not submit sensitive personal information in public comments or profile fields.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Essential cookies support sign-in, security, session continuity, and saved privacy choices.
        If optional analytics are enabled, signed-in product events are sent to Amplitude only after
        consent. Aggregate, cookie-free Plausible analytics may be enabled through deployment
        configuration. You can change your optional analytics choice using Cookie settings in the
        footer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Service providers</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        APX relies on service providers to host and operate the application, database, email delivery,
        authentication, abuse prevention, monitoring, analytics, and optional AI-assisted features.
        Depending on configuration and the feature used, providers may include SendGrid, Google,
        X, Twilio, Cloudflare Turnstile, AppSignal, Amplitude, Plausible, and OpenAI. Provider
        processing is governed by their own terms and privacy information. The deployment host and
        enabled providers can change; this page will be updated when the production configuration is
        settled.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        AI-assisted tools may process public source material and user-submitted records to provide a
        requested service. Do not assume that content submitted to an AI-assisted feature is
        confidential. The RSS intelligence hub stores public feed metadata and short excerpts and
        links to the original publisher; it does not reproduce full articles.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Newsletter and contact messages</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Newsletter subscriptions are recorded in APX and require confirmation through a one-time
        email link. A confirmation email is sent through the configured email provider. Contact-form
        messages are routed to the project contact address configured for the deployment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Retention, security, and international processing</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Account and contribution records are retained for platform operation, auditability, and
        abuse prevention. Technical logs and short-lived security identifiers have separate, limited
        retention periods. No Internet service can guarantee absolute security. Service providers
        may process data in countries other than your own, subject to the safeguards applicable to
        the deployment and provider.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Your choices and questions</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        You can manage optional analytics consent in the footer and unsubscribe from newsletters
        through the link in a confirmation or newsletter email. For a privacy question or request,
        contact the project using the <.link href={~p"/contact"} class="font-semibold text-apx-cyan underline">contact form</.link>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This policy describes the current application at a general level. It is not legal advice and
        should be reviewed against the final hosting, analytics, and email configuration before a
        public production launch.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
